          "id": "india-us-section301-tariffs-india-2026-11-25",
          "headline": "US proposes new tariffs on India, China, EU and 11 others over factory overcapacity",
          "summary": "The US Trade Representative proposed new Section 301 tariffs on 14 economies, including India, China, the EU, Japan and Vietnam, after an eight-month probe into excess factory capacity. China faces a proposed 20% extra duty; no rate has been given for India, which has no finished trade deal with the US. Hearings and public comments come first, so the duties are unlikely before January 2027.",
          "why_it_matters": "Indian exporters to the US could face new duties just as foreign money is flowing back into Indian shares.",
          "importance": 5,
          "lead": true,
          "verified": true,
          "note": "No rate for India yet; exact rates are due in a Federal Register notice.",
