          "id": "currency-rupee-eight-month-high-2026-11-25",
          "headline": "Rupee jumps 69 paise to 92.16 per dollar, its strongest close in eight months",
          "summary": "The rupee closed at 92.16 (provisional), up from 92.85, after touching about 92.19 late in the day. Record foreign buying of Indian shares, over $14 billion in November so far, and cheaper oil drove the gain, wiping out all of the rupee's losses this financial year. Change since last edition: closing level.",
          "why_it_matters": "A stronger rupee cuts India's oil and gold import bill but trims IT exporters' earnings.",
